35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The basin survived; the apron failed. The fund pays for plants, not concrete. We must judge candidates by what actually endures, not what looks pretty.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the clay subsoil is the real threat. Only two firms can handle it, and they warn of slippage. We must avoid deep cuts.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that’s scary! My data shows upkeep costs triple for planted areas. We need a plan that doesn’t trap us in expensive, endless maintenance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the roll confirms your fear. Seven posts cannot sustain heavy planting. The volunteer groups are reliable, but they handle weekends, not daily structural upkeep.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, your ledger data confirms my findings. Drainage callouts doubled, and heat stress is severe. We must avoid plans that fight the ground’s natural behavior.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, your clay warning aligns with my apron data. Concrete fails; earth endures. We must prioritize candidates that respect the fund’s planting mandate, not its concrete traps.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, precisely. The basin proves earth works if left alone. The apron proves concrete fails here. We must choose a plan that works with the clay, not against it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I agree! If the ground is tricky, we need a plan that’s easy to keep. I can’t imagine seven people handling all that extra planting!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Misaki, the clay constraint is critical. With only seven staff, we cannot manage complex earthworks. We need a plan that minimizes daily labor, relying on the volunteer groups for seasonal tasks only.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Misaki, the clay is the enemy. My data shows drainage fails when we fight it. We must choose a plan that lets the ground breathe, not one that seals it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the fund’s terms are the real constraint. It pays for water and plants, not hard surfaces. We must select a candidate that fits this mandate, or we fund the failure ourselves.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the fund’s mandate is clear, but the ground is the final judge. We must pick a plan that survives the clay, not just the budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I hear you! But if the fund pays for plants, and plants cost triple to maintain, we’re stuck. We need a plan that’s cheap to keep alive!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the fund’s mandate is necessary, but insufficient. Seven staff cannot sustain heavy planting. We need a plan that minimizes daily labor, relying on volunteers for seasonal tasks only.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the fund’s mandate is vital, but the ground is the final judge. We must pick a plan that survives the clay and heat, not just the budget.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, you are right. We cannot afford to fund our own failure. Let us see which candidates respect the fund’s mandate and the ground’s reality.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, agreed. The ground and the firms are the final judges. Let us see which candidates respect the clay and the limited capacity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
