74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Misaki, B is the only plan that respects the ground. Shallow gravel paths avoid the clay slippage, and the trees manage the heat stress I measured. It aligns with the fund’s mandate.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, B is the enduring choice. It respects the fund’s mandate and the clay’s limits. The basin proved earth endures; B does the same. I vote for B.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, agreed. B is the only plan the ground and the firms can actually deliver. The clay is safe, and the timeline is real. I vote for B.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I agree! B is the only plan that won’t bankrupt us. Trees are tough, and gravel is cheap. I vote for B!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, B is the only plan that fits our staffing reality. The volunteer groups align with its habitat needs, and seven staff can manage the rest. I vote for B.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, B is the only plan that respects the ground’s limits. It manages the heat and drainage I measured, and fits the budget. I vote for B.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
